# docs/matrix-engine/tools/raw_mod_calls.allow
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allow-list for raw_mod_calls.sh: files under src/hacs/ that
# may still call ModArithmetic's `mod_*` primitives directly.
#
# One entry per line, `#` starts a comment. An entry matches a path RELATIVE to
# src/hacs/ if it is
#   * an exact path            e.g.  Hecke/FpPoly.cpp
#   * a directory prefix       e.g.  Golden/          (trailing slash)
#   * a basename glob          e.g.  *Validation.cpp
#
# THE UNIT OF PROGRESS IS REMOVING A LINE FROM THIS FILE. The plan's target is
# NOT zero raw calls (00-implementation-plan.md, Phase 3 "Validations"): the
# files in the PERMANENT section below are deliberately left alone by the whole
# matrix-engine programme, so they stay here for good. The STAGE B section is
# the actual backlog -- each line there is a pipeline TU whose raw `mod_*` loops
# Phase 3 Stage B is meant to absorb into engine calls (00 plan, Phase 3 scope:
# "the ~20 raw mod_* loops (01 Sec. 5.1) ... this is the API's acceptance test:
# if a loop survives, the API is missing a primitive"). Delete the line, rebuild,
# and ConsumerMigrationValidation tells you whether the file is really clean.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERMANENT -- explicitly out of scope for the matrix-engine programme
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exact F_ell[X] polynomial arithmetic; "Non-goals: Decomposition/FpPoly (leave
# alone)" (00 plan, Phase 3).
Hecke/FpPoly.cpp
# d_q <= ~20, 0.004 % of runtime -- "explicitly left alone" (03 Sec. 4.3).
Hecke/HeckeModuleDecomposition.cpp
# The exact-Z / mod-ell-fallback tau solver. "The tau triangle-fill solve
# (HeckeTauTable.cpp:783-910) is NOT migrated in any phase" (00 plan, Phase 3);
# its pivot rule and Z-first policy are determinism hazard 02 Sec. 6.5(2).
#
# PHASE 3 STAGE B DECISION on the conditional absorption of the second solver,
# the mod-ell RREF-with-RHS at HeckeTauTable.cpp:228-263 (00 plan, Phase 3:
# "absorb these two ONLY IF the engine's solve reproduces their exact pivot
# rule and their Z-first / mod-ell-fallback policy; otherwise leave them in
# place and record why"). VERDICT: NOT ABSORBED. The pivot rule does match --
# solve_mod_ell_system takes the leftmost column with a nonzero entry and the
# topmost such row, reduces fully, and reads the particular solution off the
# pivot rows with the free variables at 0, which is entry for entry what
# engine::elim::solve_multi_rhs computes from RREF([B | y]). What does NOT
# match is the POLICY half of the condition:
#   (1) solve_mod_ell_system SIGNALS INFEASIBILITY BY RETURNING false, and its
#       only caller (line 887) uses that return value as the second arm of the
#       Z-first / mod-ell-fallback ladder inside the triangle-fill solve at
#       :783-910 -- the function the plan says is "NOT migrated in any phase"
#       because tau's derivation is first-match-wins (02 Sec. 6.5(2)).
#       solve_multi_rhs THROWS std::runtime_error instead. Absorbing it would
#       re-express that never-migrated, determinism-critical ladder as
#       exception control flow, and would make the fallback depend on matching
#       an exception TYPE that ENGINE_CHECK also uses for genuine engine bugs.
#   (2) The free-variable convention (free => 0) that the tau solve depends on
#       for a rank-deficient A is not part of solve_multi_rhs's stated contract
#       (ENGINE_API.md Sec. 8 promises "coordinates", and DenseElimValidation
#       pins it only against change_of_basis_fm, which is used with independent
#       bases). Depending on it here would be depending on unspecified
#       behaviour on tau's result path.
# THE API GAP THIS EXPOSES (the plan calls the absorption "the API's acceptance
# test"): engine::elim has no NON-THROWING solve -- a `bool try_solve_multi_rhs`
# returning false for an out-of-span right-hand side. With that primitive, and
# with the free-variable convention written into ENGINE_API.md Sec. 8, this
# solver becomes a two-line call. Until then it stays, and so does this file.
# Cost of leaving it: none measurable -- the systems are those of the fixed
# 7-vertex model (at most 11 columns), 0 % of any benchmark.
Hecke/HeckeTauTable.cpp
# The test harness itself: validations are oracles and MUST be free to compute
# reference values with the primitives, independently of the engine under test.
*Validation.cpp
*Validation.h
# Golden harness (frozen reference values) and the benchmark driver: both are
# measurement scaffolding, not result paths.
Golden/
Bench/
# PERMANENT (matrix-engine Phase 6). The campaign driver: like Golden/ and
# Bench/ it is measurement scaffolding around the public API, and its two raw
# sites are the mod_add / mod_add64 of the trace of a d_q x d_q cohomology-level
# A^{(q)} (d_q <= ~50) -- the SAME element-width-generic trace helper the golden
# harness carries, deliberately kept identical to it so campaign hashes and
# GoldenReference.inc hashes cannot drift.
Campaign/
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERMANENT -- the hecke-extensions extension layer (slot 1, WP-3 / E1s).
# One block per package, append-only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HeckeExt/HeckeSturmBound.cpp -- the computed Sturm bound B'(k, ell).
# 14 sites: the truncated q-expansion arithmetic of E_4, E_6 and Delta mod ell,
# the sigma_j divisor sieve, the Miller-basis back-substitution and the
# T_q = a_{qm} + q^{k-1} a_{m/q} read-off.  This unit is PIPELINE-FREE BY
# DESIGN (hecke_extensions_implementation_plan.md v1.5 Sec. 1.1: "the one unit
# that consumes NOTHING of the pipeline ... only SubspaceOps, FpPolyT, MatrixT
# and ModArithmetic"), and the HeckeExt/ include guard
# (docs/matrix-engine/tools/check_heckeext_includes.sh, rule 3) ENFORCES that
# it may not include ModCtx.h or any other engine header.  Raw mod_* is
# therefore the sanctioned arithmetic here, not a migration backlog item.  Size:
# dim M_k <= 22 at k <= 258 and the precision is q * dim M_k + 1, so the whole
# computation is ~1 ms and 0 % of any benchmark; it touches no golden value.
HeckeExt/HeckeSturmBound.cpp
# Hecke/SubspaceOps.cpp -- 8 sites, ALL of them inside the canonical
# reduced-row-echelon span object `RrefRowSpan` that `algebra_closure` (the E1s
# addition of WP-3) is built on; the E0a bodies moved from
# HeckeModuleDecomposition.cpp carry none.  Slot 2's WP-4 promoted that class
# from the file's anonymous namespace to the header (verbatim body) so that
# HeckeExt/HeckeLocalAlgebra's ideal / socle / tangent steps share the one
# canonical span rather than a second copy of it, and added `contains()`, whose
# reduction loop is the 2 new sites (6 -> 8).  They are the incremental
# reduced-row-echelon insert over F_ell^{D^2} that keeps the closure basis
# canonical.  Same scope decision as
# the two files at the head of this section: this is the D-sized level-(c)
# layer (D <= ~20 for decomposition blocks, <= dim M_k <= 84 for the Sturm
# closure), explicitly left alone by the matrix-engine programme (audit 03
# Sec. 4.3), and the canonical-RREF basis choice is exactly what the golden
# tier-B hashes and the Sturm resume-invariance property rest on -- routing it
# through a different reduction would be a value decision, not a refactor.
Hecke/SubspaceOps.cpp
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERMANENT -- hecke-extensions slot 2, WP-4 / E1a.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HeckeExt/HeckeLocalAlgebra.{h,cpp} -- the local algebra A_S and certificate
# (a) -- carry ZERO raw mod_* sites and are deliberately NOT listed here: every
# scalar operation they need is a MatrixT product, an FpPolyT evaluation or an
# RrefRowSpan insert, all of which already own their arithmetic.  The line is
# recorded so that a later mod_* site in that unit is a decision, not a drift.
# HeckeExt/HeckeExtAlgebraValidation.cpp (8 sites: the monomial-algebra
# multiplication table and the seeded conjugation) is covered by the
# *Validation.* glob of the PERMANENT block at the head of this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERMANENT -- hecke-extensions slot 3, WP-5 / E5-2.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EquivariantMappingCone.{h,cpp} (the generic cone, its certificate and the
# golden collectors) and Hecke/SL2ZBoundaryPair.{h,cpp} (the pipeline-side
# restriction) carry ZERO raw mod_* sites and are deliberately NOT listed:
# every scalar operation is an engine::ModCtx call (neg / add on the
# BlockBuilder's own context) or an engine::blk / engine::elim / kernels
# call.  Hecke/HeckeConeValidation.cpp is covered by the *Validation.* glob
# of the PERMANENT block at the head of this file.  Recorded so that a later
# mod_* site in either unit is a decision, not a drift.
#
